      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 10–15 at.% Ti will be substituted into equiatomic NbMoTaW to form a quinary refractory alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-modified NbMoTaW alloy will retain a single-phase BCC structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing an HCP element such as Ti into a BCC refractory alloy lowers dislocation core energy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti addition increases lattice distortion in the modified alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower dislocation core energy and Ti-induced lattice distortion increase the number of slip systems activated at room temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The altered dislocation and slip behavior caused by Ti will improve room-temperature ductility relative to untreated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti-induced atomic-level heterogeneity will promote irradiation-defect recombination.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Promoting defect recombination will reduce irradiation-induced defect accumulation and improve irradiation tolerance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 10–15 at.% Ti will not cause a significant loss of high-temperature yield strength up to 1600 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5995863::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial balance of ductility, irradiation tolerance, strength, and BCC stability will apply from room temperature to 1600 °C under reactor-relevant irradiation conditions.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive Ti addition may destabilize the BCC phase or produce unwanted precipitates.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal Ti concentration and the long-term irradiation stability of the modified alloy are not known.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis will be tested by comparing untreated NbMoTaW with Ti-modified alloys using mechanical tests, irradiation, defect characterization, and phase analysis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to improve room-temperature ductility and irradiation damage, or deterioration of high-temperature properties or phase stability, will falsify the hypothesis.",
